From 064dc5d5ea2d3af35da71bd8fd19215b8d5bcd79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:59:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sessions): reuse source-policy config reads within
 classification [daveey]

Five whys: sessions/tree routes stamp automated policy on every refresh;
classification separately loaded expanded config for automated, interactive
and root sidebar lists; default-home calls loaded the same revision three
times; existing readonly loads still validate/expand backend state; those
redundant validations need not run for every key of one classification.

Project the narrow lists together from one readonly snapshot per distinct
home, returning fresh list objects. Retain the existing loader's file/env/
managed/backend invalidation and outage behavior. Do not add a TTL, retain
whole config across calls, or change delta transport or F/G1/H3.

Proof: RED same-payload test expected 1 load and observed 3. GREEN one load.
HTTP sessions/tree include+exclude compare complete response bytes against
the pre-reuse policy algorithm. File/env/root edits and mutation isolation
are covered; typed backend outage still propagates and restores home.
13 focused consumer files pass. Full check's only remaining failure before
rebase is unrelated moved-base sidebar health; canonical ship re-gates.

Hermes-Card: t_945ae1e3b9c0a357
